<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ananassae Turing wavenumber at 2.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg field (a=0.11, b=1.15, Dv/Du=19.7) at 2.106 µm. Scaling both diffusivities by s² moves the FFT wavelength with the linear prediction (Pearson r = 0.99483, RMSE = 8.05e-8 m, KS = 0.167, six scales). Holding Du fixed, λ rises from 1.75 µm at Dv/Du = 8 to 2.26 µm at Dv/Du = 28, and σ changes from negative to positive across that grid. Equal diffusion and linear kinetics, integrated for 2000 steps, decay (std ratios 2.0e-4 and 6.5e-9) while the nominal system grows (1.73). The plate and the GIF last frame are segmented separately: circularity 0.136 versus 0.018, gray-level KS 0.222. Computer-vision similarity of the 12-frame 960×640 GIF to the plate is 94.3. Overall 87.4/100 (faithfulness 88.3, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 94b693bd2928b4d8996239b3f400b320fcf30723; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 94b693bd2928b4d8996239b3f400b320fcf30723, image/png, 549266 B, 1200×800 px, artifact_sha256 0fb2a26b4b6381d5811a0dc529528479f787e76ca19087897ea05f1228fb065d (sha256 0fb2a26b4b6381d5811a0dc529528479f787e76ca19087897ea05f1228fb065d), spec_fingerprint cb48fb2dc3693d0cac7caeab627f7cf256ca041c37d25c1fbbe642b593156101. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cb48fb2dc3693d0cac7caeab627f7cf256ca041c37d25c1fbbe642b593156101; artifact_sha256: 0fb2a26b4b6381d5811a0dc529528479f787e76ca19087897ea05f1228fb065d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ananassae_specimen.png=e3f07821c201b2b5..., datasets/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=2768c7dcb983c315...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | D. ananassae is a sequenced ananassae-subgroup species (12 Genomes Consortium 2007); geological age in this slot is 0 Ma. | Ready, Hanson and Benzer (1976) describe the retinal lattice at a scale of a few micrometres. | Gompel et al. (2005) and Wittkopp, Carroll and Kopp (2003) are the successor and predecessor pigment contexts, at 96 µm and 139 µm in this chronoseries.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.11, b=1.15, Dv/Du=19.7 and dx chosen so argmax Re σ(k) equals 2.106 µm. | Six-point diffusion-scale sweep, four-point ratio sweep, and two integrated ablations. | Activator field painted as a luminance modulation on the Wikimedia plate.; transfer_boundary: 2.106 µm is this slot's assigned detail-scale wavelength, not a published Turing-wavelength measurement on ananassae cuticle.; does_not_claim: The transverse sex comb and the optomotor-blind chiasma are not claimed as products of this 2.1 µm mode. | The adult body outline is the vendored plate, not an output of the reaction-diffusion field. | The Pearson coefficient is the wavelength-law fit, not a pixel identity between the plate and the field. | The Lean file was not executed by a Lean kernel on this machine.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: A second assessor has not scored this audit.",
        "remediation needed: Kernel-check the Lean file when a Lean 4 binary is available.",
        "remediation needed: The vendored plate is a 225×112 public-domain illustration, not a micrograph resolved at 2.1 µm.",
        "remediation needed: The wavelength Pearson coefficient is computed on the same six scales used to choose the comparison, so it is a fit rather than a held-out test." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.74e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ananassae Turing wavenumber at 2.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Multiplying both diffusivities by s² moves analytic and FFT wavelengths together across s = 0.75 to 1.50. Holding Du fixed, raising Dv/Du from 8 to 28 lengthens λ from 1.75 µm to 2.26 µm and carries σ from negative (no Turing) to positive." ;
