<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila ananassae Turing wavenumber at 2.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Drosophila ananassae)",
        "Drosophila ananassae Turing wavenumber at 2.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila ananassae morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila ananassae specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila ananassae" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: The Lean file was not executed by a Lean kernel on this machine.",
        "does_not_claim: The Pearson coefficient is the wavelength-law fit, not a pixel identity between the plate and the field.",
        "does_not_claim: The adult body outline is the vendored plate, not an output of the reaction-diffusion field.",
        "does_not_claim: The transverse sex comb and the optomotor-blind chiasma are not claimed as products of this 2.1 µm mode.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Activator field painted as a luminance modulation on the Wikimedia plate.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Six-point diffusion-scale sweep, four-point ratio sweep, and two integrated ablations.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a=0.11, b=1.15, Dv/Du=19.7 and dx chosen so argmax Re σ(k) equals 2.106 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: D. ananassae is a sequenced ananassae-subgroup species (12 Genomes Consortium 2007); geological age in this slot is 0 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Gompel et al. (2005) and Wittkopp, Carroll and Kopp (2003) are the successor and predecessor pigment contexts, at 96 µm and 139 µm in this chronoseries.",
        "reported_in_source: Ready, Hanson and Benzer (1976) describe the retinal lattice at a scale of a few micrometres.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.106 µm is this slot's assigned detail-scale wavelength, not a published Turing-wavelength measurement on ananassae cuticle." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila ananassae (Pantropical Pineapple Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-ananassae-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_ananassae_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila ananassae; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | D. ananassae is a sequenced ananassae-subgroup species (12 Genomes Consortium 2007); geological age in this slot is 0 Ma. | Ready, Hanson and Benzer (1976) describe the retinal lattice at a scale of a few micrometres. | Gompel et al. (2005) and Wittkopp, Carroll and Kopp (2003) are the successor and predecessor pigment contexts, at 96 µm and 139 µm in this chronoseries.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.11, b=1.15, Dv/Du=19.7 and dx chosen so argmax Re σ(k) equals 2.106 µm. | Six-point diffusion-scale sweep, four-point ratio sweep, and two integrated ablations. | Activator field painted as a luminance modulation on the Wikimedia plate.; transfer_boundary: 2.106 µm is this slot's assigned detail-scale wavelength, not a published Turing-wavelength measurement on ananassae cuticle.; does_not_claim: The transverse sex comb and the optomotor-blind chiasma are not claimed as products of this 2.1 µm mode. | The adult body outline is the vendored plate, not an output of the reaction-diffusion field. | The Pearson coefficient is the wavelength-law fit, not a pixel identity between the plate and the field. | The Lean file was not executed by a Lean kernel on this machine.]; phenomenon_size: 348 µm (0.0003476 m, log10=-3.459 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 348 µm to 1.06 m): 348 µm:anas-platyrhynchos-bioelectric-polarity, 1.3 mm:anas-platyrhynchos-vertex-packing, 2.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength, 4.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-clock-wavefront, 7.1 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-morphogen-condensation, 10.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-elastic-buckling, 17.6 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-flux-canalization, 23.3 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-branching-tree" ;
